            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/sensor_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 213,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Shouldn't this be wrote as \"L/min\" ?\n\n                \"LiquidFlowLPM\": \"This value shall indicate a measurement of a volume of liquid per unit of time, in liters per minute units, that flows through a particular junction.  The `ReadingUnits` property shall contain `L/min`.\","
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/sensor_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 213,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Zev Weiss",
                        "email": "zev@bewilderbeest.net",
                        "username": "zevweiss"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not entirely sure -- is there a particular reason to prefer one form over the other?  Existing units include both \"RPM\" and \"cft_i/min\"...I've got no strong opinion here, so if \"L/min\" would in fact be preferable I'm happy to change it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/sensor_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 213,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Gunnar is quoting from the Redfish spec there, so yeah, in this forum we should follow the spec.\n\nIf we don't like what the spec says, the DMTF forum would be where we'd effect that change."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/sensor_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 213,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Zev Weiss",
                        "email": "zev@bewilderbeest.net",
                        "username": "zevweiss"
                    },
                    "message": "Ah -- sorry, for some reason that didn't register, thanks for the clarification.  (Now fixed.)"
                }
            ],
